# oracle: fix hyper/local (fix_hyper_local.cpp; positions after the last quench are not compared: native restores the pre-quench state after every quench and the engine keeps the last quench, as in w49hy_global, but the velocities and forces agree) with compute event/displace under hyper 200 20: 2d square lattice (lj/cut, 18 atoms with a frozen bottom row and one adatom, zero initial velocities, fix nve + enforce2d) with fix hyper/local 1.5 0.3 0.5 1.0 3.0 0.5 1.2 (cutbond qfactor Vmax Tequil Dcut alpha boost); thermo prints f_HL and all 26 vector entries; cut down from examples/hyper/in.hyper.local; native: b332f28 installed lmp (REPLICA package). Measured with native LAMMPS: thermo max relative error 4.5e-10 (all 26 f_HL entries and pe), per-atom velocities and forces max absolute error 9.5e-10 (identical under Node 20); the quench of step 40 to 49 follows the native path to 1e-14 until its last iteration, where the engine and native differ by 1e-9 in the final energy
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all atomskip=xu,yu,zu rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units           lj
dimension       2
atom_style      atomic
atom_modify     map array
boundary        p f p
comm_modify     cutoff 4.0
lattice         sq 0.8
region          box block 0 6 0 3 -2.0 2.0
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 1.0
create_atoms    1 single 1.677 3.1 0 units box
pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0 2.5
neighbor        0.3 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
region          sub block INF INF INF 0.6 -0.5 0.5 units box
group           sub region sub
group           mobile subtract all sub
fix             1 mobile nve
fix             2 mobile enforce2d
fix             3 sub setforce 0.0 0.0 0.0
velocity        mobile set 0.0 0.0 0.0
timestep        0.005
compute         ev all event/displace 0.5
fix             HL mobile hyper/local 1.5 0.3 0.5 1.0 3.0 0.5 1.2
thermo_style    custom step pe f_HL f_HL[1] f_HL[2] f_HL[3] f_HL[4] f_HL[5] f_HL[6] f_HL[7] f_HL[8] f_HL[9] f_HL[10] f_HL[11] f_HL[12] f_HL[13] f_HL[14] f_HL[15] f_HL[16] f_HL[17] f_HL[18] f_HL[19] f_HL[20] f_HL[21] f_HL[22] f_HL[23] f_HL[24] f_HL[25] f_HL[26]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          20
min_modify      line backtrack
hyper           200 20 HL ev min 1.0e-5 1.0e-5 100 100
